analysisWe need to produce an assert statement corresponding to the comment:

```
// @@@ the string given for insertion will be present in the trie after addition, unless it's null
```

We are inside method add(String word). The comment says: the string given for insertion will be present in the trie after addition, unless it's null.

Method throws NullPointerException if word == null before any modifications. So spec: if word != null then after call, trie contains(word) == true. Also if word == null then method throws NPE, but spec may be expressed as implication: word != null => this.contains(word). However need to reflect that method returns boolean indicating if inserted new word. But spec only about presence.

We need to use \old for pre-state? We need to assert after addition that contains(word) holds, given word != null. Since contains is an observer method of the class (public boolean contains(String word)). So we can write:

assert word != null => this.contains(word);

But also need to consider that if word == null, method throws before any changes, but the assertion after method execution won't be evaluated because exception thrown; but spec can still be expressed as implication.

Thus final answer: <code>assert word != null => this.contains(word);</code>

Check syntax: need parentheses? Not necessary. Use => operator lower priority than &&, but fine.

Thus output.assistantfinal<code>assert word != null => this.contains(word);</code>
